Z||000006||Boodoggin||04-23-2000||11:39 PM||||87ECO5,<P>I was wondering did you buy those guages on ebay?  They look great!!  If you don't mind me asking how much did they cost?<BR>                          Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000007||87ECO5||04-24-2000||11:48 AM||||Boodoggin - yes, they were purchased through an auction on eBay for $15.  However, you can visit the person's website and avoid having to involve the third party.  The URL is:<P> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/anniversarygt350/wfg.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/anniversarygt350/wfg.htm</A> <P>They offer four different options:  two options for the backlit gauges, two for the reflector gauges.  Decals can be printed in either standard style or "racing" style (which I purchased).<P>On the website, you'll notice that, right after the advertisement for the backlit gauges, they warn that the decals can hinder the functionality of the gauges.<P>I believe that Sloponti purchased the same decals though I'm not sure which of the two reflector styles he got (standard or "racing")<P>Installing the decals wasn't too bad.  It involved dismantling the entire gauge cluster and painting the black faces white.  The only issue I have with them is the rivets on the faces show through (yes, WTIII, you did tell me so!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   ).<P>Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Boodoggin||04-24-2000||06:14 PM||||87ECO5,<BR>       Thanks so much for your help.  I looked at the page and decided on the same ones you have only the 120mph ones.  Whats up with that 240mph guage he has for the fiero?  I think thats a little ridiculous.  But any ways thanks again for all your help.(: <BR>||||reg||10
